# Site network schema

**Source of truth:** `site-network.md`. Do not invent pole/camera IPs. If unsure, read that file.

## SCC split

| SCC | Tailscale | Poles | Office (Port 1) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **SCC2** | `100.118.103.39` (`scc2`) | **1–4** | site-specific (often `192.168.2.x`) |
| **SCC1** | `100.96.105.106` (`scc1`) | **5–8** | `192.168.4.41/24`, gw `192.168.4.1` |

- Poles ingest only to **their** SCC VLAN `.40:9100`. Never cross-wire SCC1 ↔ SCC2.
- SCC1 managed switch (Port 2 fabric): **`172.16.1.190`** — do not reassign. SCC host alias on that fabric: `172.16.1.191`.
- Pole TSW202 = per-pole `.1` (not the SCC managed switch).

## Address pattern

`172.16.<subnet>.<host>`

| Pole | 3rd octet | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **3** | swapped with pole 3 |
| 2 | 2 | |
| 3 | **1** | swapped; Jetson/LiteBeam suffixes differ |
| 4–8 | = pole # | 5–8 = SCC1 |

### Standard last octets (poles 1–2, 4–8)

| Device | Octet |
|---|---|
| TSW202 switch | `.1` |
| Jetson J4012 | `.2` |
| Camera 1 PTZ | `.10` |
| Camera 2 bullet | `.11` |
| RFID FXR90 | `.12` |
| LiteBeam station | `.20` |
| LiteBeam AP (SCC) | `.21` |
| SCC on this VLAN | `.40` |

**There is no camera at `.3`.** Cameras are `.10` / `.11` only.

### Pole 3 exceptions (subnet `172.16.1.x`)

- Jetson `.50`, LiteBeam station `.91`, LiteBeam AP `.81`
- Switch / cameras / RFID / SCC `.40` still use standard last octets

## Quick examples

- Pole 6 bullet cam → `172.16.6.11`
- Pole 6 PTZ → `172.16.6.10`
- Pole 6 Jetson → `172.16.6.2` → `IR4_BASE_URL=http://172.16.6.40:9100`
- Pole 3 Jetson → `172.16.1.50` → `http://172.16.1.40:9100`

SSH Jetson via SCC when Tailscale offline: `ssh -J scc1@100.96.105.106 user@172.16.6.2` (SCC1 poles) or `ssh -J scc2@…` (SCC2 poles).
